4 bedroom flat, located in the upper area of Calçada do Combro, in a privileged location in the centre of Lisbon, between Chiado, Bairro Alto, Santa Catarina and Bica.

Inserted on the 2nd floor of a building without a lift and with two fronts, the flat is in a habitable state, having benefited from some interventions over the years, while offering an interesting potential for modernisation and reorganisation of its spaces.

Its location, configuration and number of rooms make this property a particularly interesting option for those looking for a house in the centre of Lisbon or a property with potential for appreciation through remodelling.

The flat is currently distributed as follows:

 Living room: 17.5 m²;

 Bedroom: 10 m², with window;

 Bedroom: 9.5 m²;

 Interior bedroom: 8 m²;

 Interior bedroom: 8 m², currently open and integrated into the living room area;

 Kitchen: 12 m²;

 Canopies: 3.5 m²;

 Entrance hall: 1.5 m²;

 Hallway: 5 m²;

 Private hall: 4 m²;

 Storage area/closet: 4.5 m²;

 Pantry: 3 m²;

 Full bathroom, with shower.

The current configuration allows different possibilities of use of the rooms and has the potential for a future reorganisation of the spaces, according to the needs and project of the new owner.

The flat also has:

 Two fronts;

 Living room with two windows facing Calçada do Combro;

 Renovated window frames in the living room, with double glazing;

 Renovated bathroom;

 Wooden flooring in several rooms;

 Kitchen with window and access to a small sunroom;

 Kitchen equipped with stove, fridge freezer and washing machine;

 Gas supply currently through a bottle, with piped gas in the building;

 Plumbing of the building's water supply renovated.

Prime location

Located in the upper area of Calçada do Combro, the flat benefits from a particularly central position, between Chiado, Bairro Alto, Santa Catarina and Bica, allowing you to enjoy some of the most emblematic places in Lisbon on foot.

A location that allows you to make most of your day-to-day trips on foot, benefiting from a wide range of traditional shops, supermarkets, restaurants, cafes, services, cultural spaces and public transport.

 Bica a few minutes walk away;

 Santa Catarina/Adamastor Viewpoint about 5 minutes walk;

 Luís de Camões Square about 5 minutes walk;

 Chiado and Bairro Alto in the vicinity;

 Baixa-Chiado Metro Station within walking distance;

 Cais do Sodré accessible on foot;

 Tram 28 and several public transport links in the area;

 Wide range of shops, restaurants, supermarkets and services in the surroundings.

The flat does not have private parking, however, there is a public car park in Calçada do Combro itself, open 24 hours a day and the possibility of monthly fees.

Due to its typology, distribution and location in the centre of Lisbon, this property presents itself as an opportunity for those looking for a home with versatile areas and the possibility of modernisation, as well as for those looking for a property with potential for investment and appreciation.

